Article 2. After a reconciliation agreement is reached, if any of the following circumstances exists, the People's Court may rule to suspend enforcement:
(1) all parties jointly submit the written reconciliation agreement to the People's Court;
(2) one party submits the written reconciliation agreement to the People's Court, and the other parties acknowledge it;
(3) the parties reach an oral reconciliation agreement, and the enforcement personnel record the contents of the reconciliation agreement in the transcripts, and each party signs or affixes a seal.

Article 11. Where the person applying for enforcement applies for restoration of enforcement on the ground that the party subject to enforcement fails to perform the enforcement reconciliation agreement, if upon examination the People's Court finds the ground to be established, it shall rule to restore enforcement; under any of the following circumstances, it shall rule not to restore enforcement:
(1) the application for restoration of enforcement is made after the enforcement reconciliation agreement has been fully performed;
(2) the performance period stipulated in the enforcement reconciliation agreement has not yet expired or the performance conditions have not yet been fulfilled, except where the circumstances specified in Article 578 of the Civil Code are met;
(3) the party subject to enforcement is currently performing its obligations in accordance with the enforcement reconciliation agreement;
(4) other circumstances that do not meet the conditions for restoration of enforcement.

Article 19. During enforcement, where the party subject to enforcement raises an objection in accordance with Article 225 of the Civil Procedure Law on the basis of a reconciliation agreement reached by the parties themselves but not submitted to the People's Court, or an agreement submitted to the People's Court by one party but not acknowledged by the other parties, the People's Court shall handle it separately according to the following circumstances:
(1) if the reconciliation agreement has been fully performed, rule to terminate the enforcement of the original effective legal instrument;
(2) if the performance period stipulated in the reconciliation agreement has not yet expired or the performance conditions have not yet been fulfilled, rule to suspend enforcement, except where the circumstances specified in Article 578 of the Civil Code are met;
(3) if the party subject to enforcement is currently performing its obligations in accordance with the reconciliation agreement, rule to suspend enforcement;
(4) if the party subject to enforcement fails to perform the reconciliation agreement, rule to reject the objection;
(5) if the reconciliation agreement is not established, has not taken effect, or is void, rule to reject the objection.
